course: dictionary
lesson: 928
title: Bleu: blue in French
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Bleu» is not an English word. It is French for «blue». In «le ciel bleu», it means the blue sky. Say it as «BLUH» with your lips rounded, not «bloo».
explain: French colour words usually come after the noun and change to match it. «une robe bleue» uses bleue because robe is feminine. «les yeux bleus» uses bleus because yeux is plural. Ask yourself: is the noun feminine, plural, or both?
explain: On English menus, «bleu» or «blue» describes a steak cooked very rare, only seared on the outside. Don't mix this up with the colour. The context, a menu and a steak, tells you which meaning is meant.
fact: Bleu is French, and it means blue.
fact: «Bleu» is said «BLUH» with rounded lips, and «bleue» sounds the same.
fact: The French flag is «bleu, blanc, rouge», which are blue, white and red, in that order from the flagpole.
fact: «Cordon bleu» means top-class cooking.
fact: On a menu, «bleu» can mean a steak cooked very rare, only seared outside.
exercise: In the French flag «bleu, blanc, rouge», which colour comes first from the flagpole? | Red | *Blue | Green | White
exercise: «J'ai les yeux bleus» means what? | I have blue shoes | I have red eyes | *I have blue eyes | I have green eyes
exercise: Why does bleus take an s in «les yeux bleus»? | Because bleu is an English word | Because it comes first in the sentence | *Because yeux is plural | Because it is a cooking word
test: Why is bleue used in «une robe bleue»? | Because robe is plural | *Because robe is feminine | Because it describes a steak | Because blue is an English word
test: What does «cordon bleu» mean? | *Top-class cooking | A very rare steak | The French flag | A blue cheese
exam: On an English menu, «bleu» describes what? | A dessert with cream | A cold drink | *A steak cooked very rare, only seared on the outside | A bowl of hot soup
